  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Brazilian government recently secured the approval of the base text for its proposed fiscal adjustment project in the Chamber of Deputies. The legislative process involved intense political articulation, with reports noting that members of the Centrão bloc aligned with the administration amidst expectations regarding cabinet appointments and legislative amendments. The discussions surrounding the bill also addressed concerns about potential budgetary restrictions and the necessity of balancing fiscal stability with the preservation of social programs. Gabriel Galípolo, president of the Central Bank, has publicly stated that a fiscal adjustment is both necessary and achievable without implementing absolute cuts to social policies. The progress of this legislation follows behind-the-scenes negotiations between government leaders and various political factions to ensure broad support and to manage potential resistance during the voting process.",
